Good work on #7343. One more piece goes on the same branch before the PR: #7393 (read it with `gh issue view 7393 --json title,body`). In failure_handlers.rs ~200, BindingProof::Open returns open_shape without classifying the body, so non-empty `if err != nil { return err }` branches are open gaps labeled syntax_recovery; BuiltinProof::Open (~186) does the same. Design (decided): hooks report the handler-identity proof (exact or open) and the body shape separately; the SHARED relation code in crates/bifrost-rql/src/structural/search/failure_handler_state.rs decides the row:
- identity open + non-empty body -> verdict nonempty, with the row's proof field marked inexact (find how `proof` is derived in make_value ~76; the policy filters `proof eq exact`), and no FailureHandlerDerivationIncomplete diagnostic;
- identity open + empty body -> unknown, as now;
- syntax recovery, missing body -> unknown, as now.
Apply this through the shared path so Rust native failure branches (rust_failure_handler_body_shapes) follow the same rule; check what the Rust hook does today and say whether its answers move. Add a distinct gap label for the identity gap (not syntax_recovery). Check every other consumer of failure-handler-state rows (grep RQL and policies) for whether a nonempty row with inexact proof changes their answer.
The same token `-7343-go-static-type-failure-branches` covers this if it stays query-time; if Rust answers move, say so and I will ask the coordinator about a separate token. Tests: extend your goldens with an unproven non-empty branch (decided) and an unproven empty branch (open), tagged `#[hardwon("#7393: ...")]`; rerun the 18 empty-handler goldens, the focused libs and Clippy. Then rerun the mux oracle case both variants as before and report the open-branch count before and after this commit, and whether the run is now complete. Commit separately with a multiline message ending `Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>`. No push.

Parent follow-up: the pre-ready master merge for #7507 and #7470. 61f0abcc approved both; 44b46942's Go re-review of 6ed27aa672 and 1292509a31 is still running, so keep those heads intact on the remote: commit locally and do not push.

1. In .mj/lanes/7471-go-shortvar (branch 7471-go-short-var-redeclaration, head 6ed27aa672), run git fetch origin, then git -c rerere.enabled=false merge origin/master (58db11a000 or newer); no rebase. git merge-tree predicts conflicts in:
   - crates/bifrost-go-analysis/src/analyzer/go/mod.rs and crates/bifrost-rust-analysis/src/analyzer/rust/mod.rs, where master added LanguageSupport items next to your lexical_definitions_are_authoritative opt-outs;
   - crates/bifrost-semantic/src/analyzer/semantic/icfg.rs;
   - crates/bifrost-policy/src/units.rs.
   Resolve each by keeping both sides. For the code files, diff each side against the merge base before choosing, so that no master addition is lost and none of ours is reverted. For icfg.rs, keep all of master's comment lines plus ours, and the literals v48/v47. Master is at v45/v44. If master is at or above v48/v47 when you merge, stop and tell me. For units.rs, take master's whole token line and append yours (-7471-go-short-var-redeclaration), and do the same in the test list.
2. Merge the new #7507 head into .mj/lanes/7343-go (branch 7343-go-failure-handler-typed-nil), resolving the same way: the prerequisite's tokens first, then -7343-go-static-type-failure-branches and -7393-unproven-nonempty-failure-branches.
3. Validate the merged #7470 head. It contains #7507, so one run covers both:
   - the Go and RQL lib tests you ran (286);
   - the 152 root tests through uv Python 3.12 with python,devtools;
   - the token test;
   - Clippy -D warnings on the libs you touched;
   - fmt and pack drift.
   Also compile-check the #7507 head alone (cargo check on the touched crates is enough).
   If master's change to the Go or Rust LanguageSupport impl interacts with your hook (for example, a new method with the same purpose), report it instead of picking a design.
4. Report both local heads, the conflict resolutions (one line each), the test counts and the log paths. If 44b46942 requests changes, I will send them to you to apply on top.

Parent follow-up: Go review round 3 on #7470 (7b73ea4cb5). One P1; everything else passed. The reviewer confirmed:
- the type-switch, variadic, type, receiver-formal, const, receive and range shapes;
